     1,
     "I don&#39;t know anything about Matern covariance, but the error\r<br>you&#39;re getting below is because you need to include a library\r<br>that defines size_t, such as &lt;cstddef&gt;.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>&gt; On Mar 25, 2017, at 11:04 PM, andre.pfeuffer via Stan users mailing list &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stan-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Hi,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I want to do a little exercise to enhance Stan math library by the\r<br>&gt; Matérn covariance matrices, in same fashion of Stan&#39;s cov_exp_quad\r<br>&gt; function. \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; See a definition here:\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mat%C3%A9rn_covariance_function\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mat%25C3%25A9rn_covariance_function&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792458059700000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0aFg4AhLFZiB4kVBVvw8a5\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mat%C3%A9rn_covariance_function</a>\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I only want to implement given the 3 cases for nu in {1/2, 3/2, 5/2}.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I checked out Stan math library:\r<br>&gt; $ git clone <a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/math\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/math&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792458059701000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1NL991kwoIFseFITNGqlAr\">https://github.com/stan-dev/math</a>\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;  in the makefile, I change the CC variable to g++.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Then I executed:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; $ make test-headers\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; gives me however:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; In file included from &lt;command-line&gt;:0:0:\r<br>&gt; ./stan/math/prim/arr/fun/promote_elements.hpp: In static member function ‘static std::vector&lt;T&gt; stan::math::promote_elements&lt;std::vector&lt;T&gt;, std::vector&lt;S&gt; &gt;::promote(const std::vector&lt;S&gt;&amp;)’:\r<br>&gt; ./stan/math/prim/arr/fun/promote_elements.hpp:30:14: error: ‘size_t’ was not declared in this scope\r<br>&gt;          for (size_t i = 0; i &lt; u.size(); ++i)\r<br>&gt;               ^\r<br>&gt; ./stan/math/prim/arr/fun/promote_elements.hpp:30:14: note: suggested alternatives:\r<br>&gt; In file included from /usr/include/c++/5/bits/stl_algobase.h:59:0,\r<br>&gt;                  from /usr/include/c++/5/vector:60,\r<br>&gt;                  from ./stan/math/prim/arr/fun/promote_elements.hpp:5,\r<br>&gt;                  from &lt;command-line&gt;:0:\r<br>&gt; /usr/include/x86_64-linux-gnu/c++/5/bits/c++config.h:196:26: note:   ‘std::size_t’\r<br>&gt;    typedef __SIZE_TYPE__  size_t;\r<br>&gt;                           ^\r<br>&gt; /usr/include/x86_64-linux-gnu/c++/5/bits/c++config.h:196:26: note:   ‘std::size_t’\r<br>&gt; In file included from &lt;command-line&gt;:0:0:\r<br>&gt; ./stan/math/prim/arr/fun/promote_elements.hpp:30:28: error: ‘i’ was not declared in this scope\r<br>&gt;          for (size_t i = 0; i &lt; u.size(); ++i)\r<br>&gt;                             ^\r<br>&gt; make/tests:78: recipe for target &#39;stan/math/prim/arr/fun/promote_elements.hpp-test&#39; failed\r<br>&gt; make: *** [stan/math/prim/arr/fun/promote_elements.hpp-test] Error 1\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I stuck here already. :-(\r<br>&gt; Any ideas?\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Andre\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
